[{:db/id "q-120831/selection/eff549b88f0dad60b4aaf57a41812ed8f8a24b530f6b82e0efa8a15dca6852b6" :answer/id #uuid "7d7d5dd2-7d5f-5feb-bf0d-d1d7c1317419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" :answer/id #uuid "c9df5b26-cbd5-5a17-9996-b34a3fc56473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831/selection/f34afcd1d8d06e16f767da9737fea297f9b48d4af4bb29ac0a317e64a3a131e9" :answer/id #uuid "70fa96d4-21ca-5555-abcb-67429b34cd97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831/selection/e983a3acef4246594c7c60522bdb0d85ed6924356b3a7dae378b4cc95ed4f927" :answer/id #uuid "ff8645aa-a0cf-52cb-869e-f3538acbfe43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831/selection/4c51e084e6253614e5c4efd2c8489e6900ae5b8c4e1204f11752d4e103d95983" :answer/id #uuid "35f300b6-87e7-500b-93a9-480fc9785e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5978ec59-872a-50fd-ab3f-d93edd808c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120831/selection/4c51e084e6253614e5c4efd2c8489e6900ae5b8c4e1204f11752d4e103d95983" :answer-field/choices ["q-120831/selection/eff549b88f0dad60b4aaf57a41812ed8f8a24b530f6b82e0efa8a15dca6852b6" "q-120831/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" "q-120831/selection/f34afcd1d8d06e16f767da9737fea297f9b48d4af4bb29ac0a317e64a3a131e9" "q-120831/selection/e983a3acef4246594c7c60522bdb0d85ed6924356b3a7dae378b4cc95ed4f927" "q-120831/selection/4c51e084e6253614e5c4efd2c8489e6900ae5b8c4e1204f11752d4e103d95983"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120831" :question/id #uuid "27d0bfd5-252f-58a2-8671-dfd467885e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120831" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{2}{5}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})=0.411\\,516…≈0.411\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0.411\\,5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.411\\,5.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.411\\,5.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.411\\,5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/ab3de51a23485b1776e014768b0775315694cd1147eb2772f71323d4d097dee2.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -0.411\\,5 \\\\  & ≈2.730\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈0.411\\,5\\cdot 2.730\\,1≈1.1,\n$$\n\nrounded to $1$ decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aecfac4d-b8c4-5591-b623-0fa8c192ac80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938/field-1/9b6783aca2d6ef79b1d01f4b45f9cad932ac916cf5326206da9f4d74693258e8" :answer/id #uuid "a7219c70-c22e-552a-a969-15b8ac036b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938/field-1/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" :answer/id #uuid "bd3aa92e-4445-50fb-bad9-e9e21ece1c37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "32648c8d-00f1-531e-96cd-6ac146373d0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331938/field-1/9b6783aca2d6ef79b1d01f4b45f9cad932ac916cf5326206da9f4d74693258e8" :answer-field/choices ["q-331938/field-1/9b6783aca2d6ef79b1d01f4b45f9cad932ac916cf5326206da9f4d74693258e8" "q-331938/field-1/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938/field-2/5d82d3405d35cad3389a01eccd9c1e95c5305a27c9d9c2505cc5ae44484e4a24" :answer/id #uuid "2f96d9ac-1505-5220-94fc-6517a09d1cef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3ca7385-2c82-591c-9d95-d1ebbe288501" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-331938/field-2/5d82d3405d35cad3389a01eccd9c1e95c5305a27c9d9c2505cc5ae44484e4a24" :answer-field/choices ["q-331938/field-2/5d82d3405d35cad3389a01eccd9c1e95c5305a27c9d9c2505cc5ae44484e4a24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331938" :question/id #uuid "11dd0979-73bf-536a-b52c-17378c4b7ce9" :question/math-academy-id "q-331938" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{2}{3})=-0.729\\,727…≈-0.7297\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-0.7297$ is not in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ To get the first solution that's within the required domain, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-0.7297.$ To do this, we simply add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-0.7297+2\\pi ≈5.5535\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/4a49f40b94a408ea0094eb9f8fd065622e2aad91e56c2eba24071442d0d32e4c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.7297 \\\\  & ≈3.8713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈3.9,\\,x≈5.6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331938/field-1" "q-331938/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aecfac4d-b8c4-5591-b623-0fa8c192ac80"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332377/field-1/0dcf700800b055b31767fdc86c8e47a75f2d7b6155778dc97b3e55be2443dcfa" :answer/id #uuid "db41bb04-d31c-53bc-b850-081e17600da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332377/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b488967e-5cc0-58bc-9eb8-379983710841" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332377/field-1/0dcf700800b055b31767fdc86c8e47a75f2d7b6155778dc97b3e55be2443dcfa" :answer-field/choices ["q-332377/field-1/0dcf700800b055b31767fdc86c8e47a75f2d7b6155778dc97b3e55be2443dcfa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332377/field-2/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "348ba320-4afc-5a66-82f2-62a2fd8ad60e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332377/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "036d78bd-2f45-567e-801a-d3ea340eb2de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332377/field-2/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer-field/choices ["q-332377/field-2/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332377" :question/id #uuid "65d13828-e711-5e04-8268-75cd05d3d258" :question/math-academy-id "q-332377" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ lies inside the domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{30}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/1b1a3d9a84ba0d6da8d5c2c21a91a6027b1b57e520be7c886ecf5da1a9de1ee0.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are:\n\n$$\nx=-{150}^{∘},\\,x=-{30}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332377/field-1" "q-332377/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f4d12d-55f3-5551-a993-70590cc67cb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322/field-1/0157e3ba26cc2f738da2215b5803ac734a6b702969f18e143c65478cef62430d" :answer/id #uuid "8bd4a1d7-ff23-57d3-ba3d-60b1e5227d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322/field-1/86646dfdd34dd99b12d8b2667f99ce75f934e650a9b069751cbcf304e9fbea94" :answer/id #uuid "bd465e0e-392a-5be9-9eb7-77867552c29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "129b1829-78a7-56bf-afc2-bfc95b6608fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336322/field-1/0157e3ba26cc2f738da2215b5803ac734a6b702969f18e143c65478cef62430d" :answer-field/choices ["q-336322/field-1/0157e3ba26cc2f738da2215b5803ac734a6b702969f18e143c65478cef62430d" "q-336322/field-1/86646dfdd34dd99b12d8b2667f99ce75f934e650a9b069751cbcf304e9fbea94"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322/field-2/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65" :answer/id #uuid "a11aba01-28c6-5362-8fa2-8ac3e880847f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce932f35-83c3-5a01-89bb-ab4d020b9137" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336322/field-2/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65" :answer-field/choices ["q-336322/field-2/439807d5585b48d42ced16b8185146af0ba13f97f0dbd23012170827d5b67e65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336322" :question/id #uuid "0d66e8d7-a2af-5c95-a229-af9a46e09090" :question/math-academy-id "q-336322" :question/problem "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1=0,$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{3})=-0.339\\,836…≈-0.3398\n$$\n\nSince $-0.3398$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.3398.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/ed9b300e3f4f79298feba6a2d61347d938ce64d7100ad7b0696e13dbe2a65238.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.3398 \\\\  & ≈3.4814\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & ≈3.4814-2\\pi ≈-2.8018\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈-2.8,\\,x≈-0.3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336322/field-1" "q-336322/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28f4d12d-55f3-5551-a993-70590cc67cb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336511/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "10f23361-57db-5978-a455-1b0d0f5390fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336511/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "755c8fdc-977e-5c20-ba7e-6da38c7287d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336511/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer-field/choices ["q-336511/field-1/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336511" :question/id #uuid "d5095206-b0b3-51e4-b2b3-be06116f09b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-336511" :question/problem "Find the exact solution to the equation  $2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\sqrt{2}=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$ Give your answer in degrees.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)={90}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${90}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{∘}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its maximum values at:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nSince the domain $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ is one period, and we have already found one maximum value in this period, we conclude that $x={90}^{∘}$ is the only solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336511/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6fa751e-c9a4-5f02-b858-d841f0e6ce70"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336511"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
